tr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]<span data-text=\"τελευτᾶ\" data-n=\"70\" data-lemma=\"τελευτάω\">ΤΕΛΕΥΤΑ</span><span data-text=\"δὲ\" data-n=\"75\" data-lemma=\"δέ\">ΔΕ</span>[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]<span data-text=\"Σεπτεμβρίων\" data-n=\"85\" data-lemma=\"September\">ΣΕΠΤΕΜΒΡΙΩΝ</span><span data-text=\"ἐνθάδε\" data-n=\"90\" data-lemma=\"ἐνθάδε\">ΕΝΘΑΔΕ</span><span data-text=\"κῖτε\" data-n=\"95\" data-lemma=\"κεῖμαι\">ΚΙΤΕ</span><span data-text=\"μόνανδρος\" data-n=\"100\" data-lemma=\"μόνανδρος\">ΜΟΝΑΝΔΡΟΣ</span></span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "apparatus",
      "html": "<h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span class=\"line 1\">line.1: <span>[ἀγορασία Π]αλλαδίου Ferrua; [μνημεῖον Γενν]αδίου CIG IV 9497; ... [Π]αλλαδίου IG XIV 530b</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"line 2\">line.2: <span>[συμβίου τ]ῆς Πελαγίας Ferrua; [συμβίου --- ] Πελαγίας CIG IV 9497; --- τ]ῆς Πελαγίας IG XIV 530b</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"lines 2-3\">lines.2-3: <span>ἐ[γέ|νετο Πελαγία] Ferrua; ἐ[γ|γένηθη] CIG IV 9497 ἐ[|γένηθη] IG XIV 530b</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"line 4\">line.4: <span>[--- ίων] CIG IV 9497</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"lines 4-5\">lines.4-5: <span>δ[ὲ | --- Σε]πτεμβρίων Ferrua; δ[ε τῇ πρὸ --- CIG IV 9497, IG XIV 530b (vel μηνὶ Σε]πτεμβρίω)</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"line 6\">line.6: <span>[ἐνθάδε κῖτ]ε μόνανδρο[ς] Ferrua; --- ] ἐμὸν ἄνδρ CIG IV 9497; κ]ὲ μόνανδρος IG XIV 530b</span></span></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "translation",
      "html": "<h2>English translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5187-5163\">Marta Fogagnolo</a></p>  <p>Purchase by Palladios, the husband of Pelagia. Pelagia was born 11 days before the Kalends of … and died on … September. Here lies, having had only one husband.</p>  "
    },
    {
      "id": "commentary",
      "html": "<h2>commentary</h2>  <p> The funerary inscription includes reference to the purchase of the tomb by the husband of the deceased, <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Παλλάδιος</span>, with the presence of the noun <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">ἀγορασία</span> (restored) and the genitive of the purchaser, following a formula more widespread at Syracuse, but also attested at Catania (cf. SEG 4.60, JIWE I 150). For the deceased <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Πελάγια</span> (the name is also attested in Syracuse, ASSiracusano 1956, 57), both her date of birth (ll. 2-3) and date of death (ll. 4-5) are indicated, while the final closing expression with <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">ἐνθάδε κεῖται</span> contains the information that Pelagia had only one husband in her lifetime: on the epithet <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">μόνανδρος</span> used in epitaphs to emphasize a woman's virtue, and other epithets highlighting conjugal fidelity and love, see Grandinetti 2006, 35-36 (for <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">μόνανδρος</span> used in another Sicilian epitaph, see IG XIV 191, from Syracuse).</p>  "
    },
    {
      "id": "bibliography",
      "html": "<h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> Gualtherus 1624 [1625] 41 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001931\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001931</a>  </li><li> Kirchhoff 1877 9497 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001249\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001249</a>  </li><li> Kaibel 1890 <a href=\"https://clio.columbia.edu/catalog/6873760\" target=\"_blank\">530b</a>  <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072</a>  </li><li> Ferrua 1989 no.433 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001995\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001995</a>  </li></ul>  <ul><li> Grandinetti 2006 35-36 </li></ul>  "
    },
